{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And he begot in his likeness, after his image.</b> The meaning: since Cain and Abel were born with the aspect of evil prevailing, close to the practice of evil, whereas this son was far from the aspect of evil — for the defilement had already been purged — therefore it says <b>in his likeness</b>, etc. Further, since the first two both died — Abel immediately and at once, Cain with the destruction of the generation of the Flood — and from Seth the world was established, therefore it says <b>in his likeness, after his image</b>: a man from whom the structure of the world would be built. Moreover, he too is a faithful father, namely the holy one; go forth and learn from Levi (Tanhuma, Yitro)."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:39:19.851075043Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}